.TH YABI 1 "2026-11-01" "yabi 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
yabi \- yet another bootsplash implementation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yabi
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yabi
shows a boot splash on the Linux framebuffer, and lets the boot scripts drive
it.
.PP
The first call starts
.BR fbv (1)
with a control socket and leaves it running. Every later call sends one
command to it and exits. There is no daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR start " [\fItheme\fR]"
Start fbv with the animation of the theme, and wait until fbv answers. The
default theme is \fBdefault\fR. A theme in \fBprogress\fR mode starts on its
first frame.
.TP
.BI progress " percent"
Move a progress animation to \fIpercent\fR (0 to 100). When moving forward,
the animation steps through its frames at its own pace.
.TP
.BI frame " n"
Show frame \fIn\fR of the animation.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume
Stop and restart the animation.
.TP
.BI show " file"
Switch to another image or animation.
.TP
.BI theme " theme"
Switch to another theme.
.TP
.B status
Print the current frame, the frame count and whether the animation is paused.
.TP
.B ping
Exit 0 when the splash is running.
.TP
.B quit
Close the splash and wait until fbv has exited. The framebuffer is then free.
.TP
.BR watch " [\fIdir\fR...]"
Follow the boot in the background and move the progress, until the splash is
gone. What it follows depends on the system:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
It follows the executable \fBS??*\fR scripts of the init directories as they
run, in the order of the directories and then of the names. The default
directory is /etc/init.d.
.IP \(bu 2
Under OpenRC, it follows the started services of the sysinit, boot and default
runlevels instead.
.PP
It changes nothing in init or rc. \fBS00yabi\fR starts it.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIpath\fR"
The control socket. The default is /run/yabi.sock, or \fB$YABI_SOCKET\fR when
it is set.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fbv " \fIpath\fR"
The fbv program to start. The default is \fBfbv\fR from \fB$PATH\fR, or
\fB$YABI_FBV\fR when it is set.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-themes " \fIdir\fR"
The directory that holds the themes.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIms\fR"
How long to wait for fbv, in milliseconds. The default is 3000.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-graphics
For \fBstart\fR: leave the console in text mode.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-retain
For \fBquit\fR: keep the splash on the screen and the console in graphics
mode, for the program that takes over the display.
.SH THEMES
A theme is a directory that holds \fBtheme.conf\fR and an animation. You give
a theme by its name, or by a path that contains a slash.
.PP
.nf
# comment
animation = boot.gif   # relative to the theme directory
mode = progress        # progress or loop
scale = none           # none, shrink or fit
.fi
.PP
In \fBprogress\fR mode, the animation holds the frame set by \fBprogress\fR.
With an animation of 101 frames, each percent has its own frame.
.PP
In \fBloop\fR mode, the animation plays freely.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command is done.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
The splash is not running.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
yabi start
yabi progress 30
yabi quit
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbv (1)
